# agent-tools: codex — a FROM-scratch OCI image whose whole root filesystem is
# /bin/codex (codex's upstream static-pie musl binary) and /bin/labctl (built
# static from this repo). Pure payload: no shell, no userland, no base, and
# NEVER run as a container. The container runner (#205) mounts it read-only into
# an operator-chosen dev container via `podman run --mount type=image,...,dst=/opt/lab`
# and prepends /opt/lab/bin to PATH.
#
# Unlike claude, codex's linux musl build is static-pie with no PT_INTERP and no
# DT_NEEDED — it runs on any base as-is, so nothing is patched and no loader is
# bundled. The /opt/lab mount is still the runner's contract for PATH resolution
# (ADR-0051, docs/ops.md § "Agent-tools images"), but for codex it carries no
# baked-in path dependency. Consumers pin the immutable @sha256: digest, not the
# human-facing version tag.

# ---- Stage: labctl — static pure-Go binary built from the working tree -------
# Identical to Containerfile.claude's labctl stage (see that file for rationale):
# CGO_ENABLED=0 matches the Makefile; untagged build uses the webui placeholder,
# so no embedded SPA dist is needed.
FROM docker.io/library/golang:1.26-alpine AS labctl
WORKDIR /src
COPY go.mod go.sum ./
RUN go mod download
COPY . ./
RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags='-s -w' -o /out/labctl ./cmd/labctl

# ---- Stage: codex — verify, extract, sanity-run ------------------------------
FROM docker.io/library/alpine:3.22 AS codex

# No defaults: build.sh always passes both from versions.env. A missing arg must
# fail the build, never silently accept something else.
ARG CODEX_VERSION
ARG CODEX_SHA256_X64_MUSL_TGZ

# The pinned release tarball is fetched, sha256-verified, and cached by
# build.sh into the build context (see its fetch_artifact rationale). COPY it,
# RE-verify the sha256 in-stage, then extract: the tar member is named
# codex-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl; rename it to /out/codex.
COPY containers/agent-tools/artifacts/codex-${CODEX_VERSION}-x86_64-linux-musl.tar.gz /tmp/codex.tar.gz
RUN mkdir -p /out \
    && echo "${CODEX_SHA256_X64_MUSL_TGZ}  /tmp/codex.tar.gz" | sha256sum -c - \
    && tar -xzf /tmp/codex.tar.gz -C /tmp \
    && mv /tmp/codex-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl /out/codex \
    && chmod 755 /out/codex

# Build-time sanity run. codex is static-pie with no interpreter, so it runs
# here as-is (and identically once injected) — no patching needed.
RUN /out/codex --version

# ---- Final: pure payload -----------------------------------------------------
FROM scratch
# ARG must be redeclared in this stage to reach the version label below.
ARG CODEX_VERSION
COPY --from=codex /out/codex /bin/codex
COPY --from=labctl /out/labctl /bin/labctl
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.title="agent-tools: codex" \
      org.opencontainers.image.description="Self-contained codex (static-pie linux musl) plus static labctl, mounted read-only at /opt/lab for injection into an operator-chosen dev container." \
      org.opencontainers.image.source="https://git.cloonar.com/Cloonar/coding-lab" \
      org.opencontainers.image.version="${CODEX_VERSION}" \
      com.cloonar.lab.provider="codex"
